        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-1121_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-1121_47399_lbl" />
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-02_47034_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><div class="Section0"><p><span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none">Schedule Page 102 Line No.:1 Column: a</span></p><p><span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none"><br /></span></p><p class="_Normal_"><span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none">The following are the intermediary companies in the chain of ownership between Energy Transfer LP (DE) and ET CC Holdings LLC (DE):</span></p><p class="_Normal_"><span lang="en-US" style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal">Energy Transfer </span><span lang="en-US" style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal">LP (DE) owns 100% of ET CC Holdings LLC (DE). ET CC Holdings LLC (DE) owns 100% of West Texas Gulf Pipe Line Company LLC (DE).</span><br /></p><p class="_Normal_"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal"><br /></span></p><p style="text-align: left; page-break-inside: auto; page-break-after: auto; page-break-before: avoid; line-height: 107.916664%; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"><span style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; line-height: 107.916664%"><br /></span></p><p style="text-align: left; page-break-inside: auto; page-break-after: auto; page-break-before: avoid; line-height: 107.916664%; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"><span style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; line-height: 107.916664%"><br /><br /></span></p></div></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-126_47035_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">Cash management program with Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-495_47372_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $3.4 million is included in Account(s) 600.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1092_47190_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">Cash management program with Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1121_47399_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p>In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $1,708,448 are included in line 10, interstate operating revenue. These revenues represent a one-time event and are not representative of future revenues.</p><p> </p><p>The cost of service results were calculated using the Cost of Service Model. This Model calculates cost of service using the Trended Original Cost methodology promulgated by the FERC in Opinion No. 154-B, 31 FERC  61,377 (1985), as modified and clarified by subsequent rulings.</p></div></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>